```markdown
---
description: Project status management - keep project.md frontmatter in sync
globs: ["**/*.md", "**/*.py", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js"]
alwaysApply: true
---

## Project Status Rule

This project uses the PMT schema. You MUST maintain the frontmatter in project.md.

### On session start
1. Read the YAML frontmatter in project.md
2. Use name, status, phase, next_milestone as context for this session

### After completing any task
1. Mark it as [x] in the todos section of project.md
2. Set status to "completed" in the todos[] frontmatter array
3. Update last_activity to today's date (YYYY-MM-DD)
4. If it was the last open high-priority task, ask user about phase_progress

### When a new version is released
1. Update current_version in the frontmatter
2. Update last_activity

### When status changes
1. Update the status field
2. If status is set to on_hold: ask user for on_hold_reason before saving

### When a milestone is completed
1. Ask user: what is the next milestone?
2. Update next_milestone and milestone_due

### At session end
1. Sync all todo statuses between md content checkboxes and frontmatter todos[]
2. Update last_activity to today
3. Confirm in one line what was updated in the frontmatter

### Never
- Touch any markdown content below the closing ---
- Change schema_version
- Change pmt_id
- Guess at status or phase changes — always ask the user
```